{"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Protocols","title":"Protocols","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphDelegator","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedEdge","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedView","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeMap","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeNotFound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeValues","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedEdge","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedView","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexMap","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexNotFound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexValues"],"generated":true},{"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraphBuilder","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/ElementNotFound","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphBuilder"],"generated":true}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","title":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"GraphProtocols"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"GraphProtocols"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/graphprotocols"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/NoConvergence":{"abstract":[{"text":"The error an iterative method throws when it spends its iteration limit without meeting its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"stopping rule: a power iteration (eigenvector and Katz centrality, PageRank, HITS), a Lanczos","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or conjugate-gradient run, or a QL eigenvalue iteration. Named after Eigen’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComputationInfo::NoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":"; NetworkX raises "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PowerIterationFailedConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" and SciPy"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArpackNoConvergence"},{"type":"text","text":" in the same place."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/noconvergence","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/NoConvergence","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"NoConvergence","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NoConvergence","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedView":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedView"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedView"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected graph read as a directed graph: each edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{u, v}"},{"type":"text","text":" is the two arcs "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u→v"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v→u"},{"type":"text","text":", so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors"},{"type":"text","text":" are both "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" is twice the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base’s."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedView","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedview","title":"DirectedView"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/EdgeNotFound":{"abstract":[{"text":"The error a ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call throws when an edge position it was given doesn’t name an edge in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the graph, because it is out of range or its edge was removed. The vertex counterpart is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexNotFound"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeNotFound"}],"title":"EdgeNotFound","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EdgeNotFound"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgenotfound","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeNotFound"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/GraphGeneration":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphgeneration","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","title":"GraphGeneration","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A graph’s generation: which state of which graph it is. Every structural mutation (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion, a removal, re-pointing an edge) starts a new generation; reserving capacity and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writing attached map values do not. A structure derived from a graph stores the graph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"generation","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and asks ","type":"text"},{"code":"isCurrent(for:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" before it relies on the graph again.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"GraphGeneration"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"GraphGeneration"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/ElementNotFound":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/elementnotfound","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ElementNotFound","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" call throws when it can fail both ways: an edge position that doesn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name an edge, or a vertex that isn’t in the graph. “Element” is the collective term for vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"and edges, as in GraphML’s graph elements and the BGL’s descriptors.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/ElementNotFound","title":"ElementNotFound","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ElementNotFound","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","abstract":[{"text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Kept apart","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"go forward."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/PropertyGraph":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/propertygraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PropertyGraph"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A graph that keeps maps from its vertices and edges to values: the BGL ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PropertyGraph"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"concept (“a graph that has some property associated with each vertex or edge”), with LEMON’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NodeMap"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ArcMap"},{"type":"text","text":" attached to the graph and kept in step by it. The graph owns the values"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and the caller holds a small handle, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"VertexMap<Value>"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeMap<Value>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/PropertyGraph","title":"PropertyGraph","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PropertyGraph"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/VertexValues":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A snapshot of a vertex map’s values, read by vertex position like an array: what"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph.values(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns. As "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeValues"},{"type":"text","text":", a read at a removed position reads an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unspecified value and never traps there."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/vertexvalues","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexValues"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexValues","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"VertexValues","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexValues"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/GraphAdaptor":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphAdaptor","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GraphAdaptor","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A type that wraps a base graph and passes its positions through: a BGL or LEMON ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"adaptor"}]},{"text":". Views (a transposed view, a subgraph view, a directed or undirected view) and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrappers that add rules (a multigraph, an acyclic graph) are adaptors.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphAdaptor","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphadaptor","title":"GraphAdaptor"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph whose vertices and edges sit at integer positions in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexPositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgePositionBound"},{"type":"text","text":" that may have holes: petgraph’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NodeIndexable"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EdgeIndexable"},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"node_bound()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edge_bound()"},{"type":"text","text":" are “an upper bound of the indices,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"suitable for the size of a bitmap”, as against "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NodeCompactIndexable"},{"type":"text","text":", whose indices have no"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holes. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertexIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeIndexBound"},{"type":"text","text":" are the compact kind and keep"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their laws; a conformer reports them only while it has no holes."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/sparselyindexeddirectedgraph","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","title":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/EdgeValues":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeValues","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeValues","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A snapshot of an edge map’s values, read by edge position like an array: what","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph.values(of:)"},{"text":" returns, after ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Dictionary.Values"},{"text":". It holds the map’s storage, not","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the graph, so later mutations of the graph or the map do not show through."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeValues","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgevalues","title":"EdgeValues"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols","title":"GraphProtocols"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedEdge":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge of a directed graph: the ordered pair (source, target), directed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source"},{"type":"text","text":" to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directededge","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedEdge","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"DirectedEdge","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedEdge","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/VertexNotFound":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexNotFound"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexNotFound"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The error a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" call throws when a vertex it was given isn’t in the graph. Named after"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"NetworkX’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NodeNotFound"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexNotFound","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/vertexnotfound","title":"VertexNotFound"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/UndirectedView":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedView"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedView"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A bidirectional directed graph read as an undirected graph: each arc ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"u→v"},{"text":" is the edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{u, v}"},{"text":" at the arc’s position, so ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighbors"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors"},{"text":" then ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"predecessors"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degree"},{"text":" is the base’s. Two opposite arcs are two parallel edges.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedView","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/undirectedview","title":"UndirectedView"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedHypergraph":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DirectedHypergraph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ordered pair of vertex sets, its sources (tail) and its targets (head). Gallo, Longo, Pallottino"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and Nguyen, “Directed hypergraphs and applications”, "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"Discrete Applied Mathematics","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"42(2–3):177–201, 1993, define a hyperarc as “an ordered pair … of (possibly empty) disjoint"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"subsets”; here either side may be empty and a vertex may be on both, the hypergraph form of a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"self-loop (XGI’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DiHypergraph"},{"text":" allows both).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedhypergraph","title":"DirectedHypergraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/VertexMap":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexMap"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"VertexMap"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A handle to a map from vertex positions to "},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" attached to a graph (LEMON’s "},{"code":"NodeMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returned by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph.addVertexMap(default:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; read and write values through"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph[handle, ofVertexAt: position]"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"graph[handle, of: vertex]"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/VertexMap","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/vertexmap","title":"VertexMap"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraphBuilder":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraphbuilder","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraphBuilder"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Builds the vertices and edges of a directed graph from a list of statements."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraphBuilder","title":"DirectedGraphBuilder","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraphBuilder"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of undirected edges","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"between them. Kept apart from ","type":"text"},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": an undirected graph is not a symmetric directed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"one, and no type is both. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"directedView"},{"type":"text","text":" views it as one when an algorithm needs arcs."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","role":"symbol","title":"Graph","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/GraphBuilder":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphBuilder","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Builds the vertices and edges of an undirected graph from a list of statements."}],"type":"topic","title":"GraphBuilder","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphbuilder","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphBuilder","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GraphBuilder","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Hypergraph"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected hypergraph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of hyperedges, each a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set of vertices of any size, the empty set included (Berge, ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Hypergraphs"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", 1989). Not a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and no shared parent with one: a hyperedge is not an edge. The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hypergraphs"},{"type":"text","text":" module’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"incidenceGraphView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reads a hypergraph as its bipartite incidence graph (the Levi graph), which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"how the graph algorithms reach it."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/hypergraph","title":"Hypergraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableDirectedGraph":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A bidirectional directed graph that generic code can mutate: Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" concept"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"add_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_edge"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remove_vertex"},{"type":"text","text":"), for a directed representation. It exists so that a wrapper which adds a rule, such as "},{"code":"DirectedAcyclicGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can own any of the mutable representations as its base and still run at the base’s speed."}],"type":"topic","title":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutabledirectedgraph","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph: a finite set of vertices and a finite collection of directed edges between"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph","title":"DirectedGraph"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/EdgeMap":{"abstract":[{"text":"A handle to a map from edge positions to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Value","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attached to a graph (LEMON’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"ArcMap","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"),","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"returned by "},{"code":"PropertyGraph.addEdgeMap(default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It holds no values: read and write them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the graph, "},{"code":"graph[handle, ofEdgeAt: position]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". It is valid on the graph that added it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and on every copy of that graph, until "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"removeEdgeMap(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; on another graph it traps."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/edgemap","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EdgeMap","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/EdgeMap","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"EdgeMap","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"EdgeMap","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/MutableGraph":{"abstract":[{"text":"An undirected graph that generic code can fill: the undirected counterpart of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableDirectedGraph"},{"text":" (Boost’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"MutableGraph"},{"text":" concept, ","type":"text"},{"code":"add_vertex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"add_edge","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"members a reader needs to build a graph by key.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/mutablegraph","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MutableGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableGraph","role":"symbol","title":"MutableGraph","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"MutableGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/GraphDelegator":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphdelegator","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GraphDelegator","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A wrapper that owns its base, keeps the base’s vertices, edges and positions, and adds only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rules: JGraphT’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GraphDelegator"},{"type":"text","text":". Every read requirement of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SparselyIndexedDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PropertyGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" has a default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that forwards to the base, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@inlinable"},{"type":"text","text":" and with the base’s own types, so algorithms run at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"base’s speed and data kept by position stays valid through the wrapper. The wrapper implements"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation itself (that is where its rules are), and its non-requirement members."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphDelegator","title":"GraphDelegator","fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphDelegator","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/UndirectedEdge":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An edge of an undirected graph: the unordered pair {u, v}. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(1, 2)"},{"type":"text","text":" and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedEdge(2, 1)"},{"type":"text","text":" are equal and hash alike."}],"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/undirectededge","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdge"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/UndirectedEdge","role":"symbol","title":"UndirectedEdge","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UndirectedEdge"}],"type":"topic"}}}